  "captions": [
    {
      "startFrame": 0,
      "endFrame": 30,
      "text": "Did you know"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 30,
      "endFrame": 66,
      "text": "France's longest border"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 66,
      "endFrame": 102,
      "text": "is with Brazil?"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 102,
      "endFrame": 144,
      "text": "In Europe, France has eight neighbors:"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 144,
      "endFrame": 192,
      "text": "Spain, Andorra, Italy, Monaco,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 192,
      "endFrame": 240,
      "text": "Switzerland, Germany,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 240,
      "endFrame": 288,
      "text": "Luxembourg and Belgium."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 288,
      "endFrame": 360,
      "text": "But its strangest borders hide in the corners."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 360,
      "endFrame": 420,
      "text": "On the Riviera sits Monaco,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 420,
      "endFrame": 495,
      "text": "wrapped by France on every side but the sea."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 495,
      "endFrame": 570,
      "text": "At just 2 square kilometers,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 570,
      "endFrame": 660,
      "text": "it's the second-smallest country in the world,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 660,
      "endFrame": 735,
      "text": "yet home to about 38,000 people —"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 735,
      "endFrame": 810,
      "text": "the most densely populated country on Earth."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 810,
      "endFrame": 885,
      "text": "Now cross the Atlantic."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 885,
      "endFrame": 960,
      "text": "6,700 kilometers from Paris"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 960,
      "endFrame": 1035,
      "text": "lies the island of Saint Martin,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1035,
      "endFrame": 1125,
      "text": "split between France and the Netherlands."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1125,
      "endFrame": 1200,
      "text": "That gives France a land border with the Dutch"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1200,
      "endFrame": 1260,
      "text": "that it doesn't have in Europe."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1260,
      "endFrame": 1335,
      "text": "Legend says the border was settled by a walking race:"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1335,
      "endFrame": 1410,
      "text": "the Frenchman drank wine, the Dutchman gin."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1410,
      "endFrame": 1485,
      "text": "Further south, on the edge of the Amazon,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1485,
      "endFrame": 1560,
      "text": "is French Guiana — a full part of France."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1560,
      "endFrame": 1635,
      "text": "It borders Suriname to the west"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1635,
      "endFrame": 1725,
      "text": "and Brazil to the south and east."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1725,
      "endFrame": 1815,
      "text": "That border runs about 730 kilometers,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1815,
      "endFrame": 1905,
      "text": "longer than France's border with Spain."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1905,
      "endFrame": 1995,
      "text": "So France's longest land border"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1995,
      "endFrame": 2070,
      "text": "is with Brazil."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2070,
      "endFrame": 2160,
      "text": "Here on the Oyapock River,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2160,
      "endFrame": 2250,
      "text": "a bridge links the French town of Saint-Georges"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2250,
      "endFrame": 2340,
      "text": "to Oiapoque in Brazil —"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2340,
      "endFrame": 2430,
      "text": "where the European Union meets South America."
    }
  ],
